{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599212-auspice-and-tribe-in-30-words-or-less","id":599212,"title":"Auspice and Tribe in 30 Words or Less","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-22T05:10:42-07:00","id":599212,"title":"Auspice and Tribe in 30 Words or Less","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I'm looking at ways to help ease players into a game and was wondering if anyone could help come up with a quick and or pithy description of each of the Auspices and Tribes that I could use to help them. 30 words max as that's quick and easy to read.<br /> <br /> This kind of thing was quite easy (and effective) for V:tR, but W:tF stumps me.<br /> <br /> E.g.: Ordo Dracul<br /> Bloody, visceral scientific occultists looking to overcome vampire weaknesses. They apply a scientific mindset to magic and the occult and use the results of experimentation to become a 'better monster'.<br /> <br /> Can anyone help? Rather than expecting the players to read all of the 5 tribe and auspice sections before deciding which one they are interested in I'd rather them to know which ones interest them from the short blurb and then read into them in more detail.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 07-22-2015, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T05:54:32-07:00","id":599273,"title":"","content":"Auspices:<br /> <br /> Irraka<br /> Go find the prey, trap him whyle your chumps arrive. You're not to be saw so much by friend or foe.<br /> <br /> Ithaeur<br /> Deal with spirits, learn from spirits, then scare the hell out off spirits, so the don't mess with the hunt.<br /> <br /> Elodoth<br /> Think. Make a strategy. Be sure everything that have to be done will be done. Damn the consequences.<br /> <br /> Cahalith<br /> Scare the hell out of prey, play the emotions of your chumps and make them best hunters.<br /> <br /> Rahu<br /> Wait. Wait. Enter Gauru. Kill. Repeat. Your chumps will bring the prey for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T06:23:14-07:00","id":599289,"title":"","content":"Blood Talons: Werewolves are apex hunters. These are the guys who hunt them. <br /> <br /> Bone Shadows: The occulists of the werewolves, they deal with spirits, like Ithaeur do, but also ghosts, which they don't. <br /> <br /> Iron Masters: The urbanised faction of werewolves. Most likely to have magitech fetishes. <br /> <br /> Hunters In Darkness: Werewolves with a particular bent towards nature. Wild man of the woods types. <br /> <br /> Storm Lords: The self-styled &quot;nobility&quot; of the werewolves. Most of the other tribes just roll their eyes. Big on standing strong in the face of adversity, honour and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T07:22:21-07:00","id":599357,"title":"","content":"As a werewolf, you'll have to fight for your life; probably on a regular basis. The Blood Talons show you how. They know how to protect yourself and those close to you; Fenris-Ur will teach you how to be an effective warrior. They also give you ways how to deal with the burning rage affecting all werewolves. The Blood Talons are the ones you approach when you don't want to wake up in the blood of your husband one day, and when you want to survive the next time the Predator Kings show up from nowhere and start biting huge chunks of flesh out of your flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T07:24:09-07:00","id":599359,"title":"","content":"This scary, hostile world of predator and prey you are now a part of? The Bone Shadows best understand how it works and how to make sense of it. They explain spirits. They tell you which places in the Shadow to avoid and where you'll be safe. Death Wolf provides you with the means of fighting your enemies with ways other than using your claws. And they also show you how to make sense of the death and pain and grief that always seems to follow the Forsaken around. They provide meaning in a world that doesn't appear to have any, at the first glance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T07:25:55-07:00","id":599362,"title":"","content":"There's a wolf in your heart, your bones and your flesh, and it'll never go away. The Hunters in Darkness know that wolf better than any other tribe. They know how to make sense of the rage, the new senses, instincts, demands of the wolf-heart. They also teach you how to hunt effectively, and how to survive when you're prey. Things like where to best hide, how to best track your prey, how to kill prey in as little time as possible are natural to the children of the Black Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T07:27:26-07:00","id":599364,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are not human. The human skin doesn't change their basic nature; but despite the wolf-heart and spirit-soul there's still a human mind. After the traumatic experience of the First Change, which more often than not, ends with lots of blood, the Iron Masters are the ones who help a young werewolf to reintegrate into the human culture and world and to reconcile wolf-heart with human-mind. They're the ones who know how a wolf hides and hunts among sheep. Red Wolf knows the spirits that hunt in the cities and close to humanity, and his children will teach you how to hunt with cunning, how to adapt to situations that cannot otherwise be dealt with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T07:48:47-07:00","id":599383,"title":"","content":"The Storm Lords don't pick you up when you're weak. They won't comfort you in your time of need. Winter Wolf does not care about your weakness and failings. The Storm Lords cannot soothe any pain you feel from the First Change or from being what you are. The Winter Wolf will instead be here in your moments of strength and endurance. His children show you how to be your best, strongest self - how to stare this cold, dark, hostile world that wants you dead at every turn, in the face, and how to make it back down with an alpha's growl. They know how to fight. They know the spirit world, the worlds of wolf and men. All of these things are part of their responsibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T08:45:36-07:00","id":599452,"title":"","content":"As for the auspices, I think they're not as complex as the tribes, so it's easier to come up with short descriptions or questions or phrases that capture what they are about. <br /> <br /> Rahu: The Moon has chosen you to be a killer. Doesn't that scare you? <br /> <br /> Cahalith: The road to glory is bright and well lit, and it always ends in doom. <br /> <br /> Elodoth: Honor cuts both ways. <br /> <br /> Ithaeur: Wisdom or madness? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T08:59:06-07:00","id":599489,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys, that's a lot of stuff pretty quickly!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T09:41:41-07:00","id":599535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599212-auspice-and-tribe-in-30-words-or-less?p=599357#post599357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a werewolf, you'll have to fight for your life; probably on a regular basis. The Blood Talons show you how. They know how to protect yourself and those close to you; Fenris-Ur will teach you how to be an effective warrior. They also give you ways how to deal with the burning rage affecting all werewolves. The Blood Talons are the ones you approach when you don't want to wake up in the blood of your husband one day, and when you want to survive the next time the Predator Kings show up from nowhere and start biting huge chunks of flesh out of your flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599212-auspice-and-tribe-in-30-words-or-less?p=599383#post599383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Storm Lords don't pick you up when you're weak. They won't comfort you in your time of need. Winter Wolf does not care about your weakness and failings. The Storm Lords cannot soothe any pain you feel from the First Change or from being what you are. The Winter Wolf will instead be here in your moments of strength and endurance. His children show you how to be your best, strongest self - how to stare this cold, dark, hostile world that wants you dead at every turn, in the face, and how to make it back down with an alpha's growl. They know how to fight. They know the spirit world, the worlds of wolf and men. All of these things are part of their responsibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both excellent descriptions, and perhaps too excellent as I still remain torn as to which Tribe is my favorite in Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T15:12:51-07:00","id":599859,"title":"","content":"Cahalith blood Talon = Mathias nyg\u00e5rd from turisas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T15:13:56-07:00","id":599860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599212-auspice-and-tribe-in-30-words-or-less?p=599859#post599859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cahalith blood Talon = Mathias nyg\u00e5rd from turisas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most power metal front-men fit as Cahalith Talons, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T15:17:02-07:00","id":599864,"title":"","content":"Blood talons: warriors. Their body is a weapon, and the only prey good enough is themselves. <br /> <br /> bone shadows: the worlds secrets can be found in the shadow, and only the spirits know them.<br /> <br /> Hunters in darkness: the purity of nature needs to be maintained. Hosts corrupt and warp it.<br /> <br /> Iron masters: humanity represents a problem that must be culled. They go and adapt where they must. <br /> <br /> Storm lords: spirits violated the border in fathers time and he culled them. We do the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T03:39:38-07:00","id":600331,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Blood Talons</b></u><br /> All are warriors<br /> Rage and slaughter in their blood<br /> Hunters of werewolves<br /> <br /> <u><b>Bone Shadows</b></u><br /> Keepers of Shadow<br /> Negotiate, watch and act<br /> Pay spirits in kind<br /> <br /> <u><b>Hunters in Darkness</b></u><br /> Monsters in the dark<br /> Territory over all<br /> The hunt never ends<br /> <br /> <u><b>Iron Masters</b></u><br /> Humans innovate<br /> Werewolves cannot cling to past<br /> Adapt, change, or die<br /> <br /> <u><b>Storm Lords</b></u><br /> Hunters proud and strong<br /> Unstoppable rumbling dark<br /> Keep weakness hidden<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T03:48:49-07:00","id":600333,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Cahalith</b></u><br /> Seekers of Glory<br /> Visionaries and prophets<br /> Harrowing the prey<br /> <br /> <u><b>Elodoth</b></u><br /> Judge and messenger<br /> Social manipulators<br /> You\u2019ll do what they want<br /> <br /> <u><b>Irakka</b></u><br /> Unseen and unheard<br /> Ignorant and blissful prey<br /> Strike from the shadows<br /> <br /> <u><b>Ithaeur</b></u><br /> Shaman stands apart<br /> Delegate to the Shadow<br /> Master of spirits<br /> <br /> <u><b>Rahu</b></u><br /> To live is to fight<br /> Overwhelm, defeat the prey<br /> Your blood ends the hunt<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>